    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Josh Naylor** anchoring the offense as our primary point-producers. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) benefits from a pristine matchup against an opposing starter sporting a 7.11 xERA, while **Josh Naylor** (70.98) capitalizes on strong park factors and a favorable platoon profile. We are also aggressively deploying **Jose Caballero** (64.31) and **James Wood** (62.97); despite **Jose Caballero** hitting out of the eight-hole, his dynamic platoon edge and capacity for stolen bases\u2014a critical scarcity for our roster\u2014make him a mandatory start. **Brice Turang** (62.75) rounds out our top-tier targets, though we are tracking a 4% efficiency drag due to the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop time, which slightly caps his upside on the basepaths.\n\nThe bench decision process was narrow, with **Austin Riley** (47.29) narrowly missing the cut behind **Seiya Suzuki** (47.79). While **Austin Riley** offers superior raw power, his matchup against a sub-3.00 xERA arm significantly dampened his projected efficiency, making **Seiya Suzuki** the safer play for contact-heavy categories. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Corbin Carroll** (57.48); while his speed is vital, he is facing a pitcher with a 2.96 xERA, necessitating a conservative outlook on his counting stats today. **Carson Williams** (59.95) and **Cole Young** (58.06) remain firmly in the lineup due to favorable park factors, though we are closely monitoring lineup confirmations, as any shift down the order for **Carson Williams** would further suppress his marginal scoring profile.",
